@page "/access-denied"
@layout MarketingLayout
@* Where a signed-in account without catalog access lands. The authorization middleware answers a
   request that arrives with a redirect to the address in the cookie options, and without a page here
   that redirect goes to the handler's default, which this application does not serve: a blank 404
   where an explanation belongs. What it says is the same component the router renders for a
   navigation made inside the running application, so both ways in give one answer. *@
<AccessRefused />

@code {
    /// <summary>This page's own address, which the cookie options name rather than repeat.</summary>
    public const string Path = "/access-denied";
}
